-- title:
--   Non-toric 𝔪-torsion at p forces lower-level torsion
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $p$ with $N_0$ and $p$ non-zero, $p$ prime, and $p \nmid N_0$; fix a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$ (the predicate `LiesOverPrime`), level data $\Lambda$ for $(N_0,p,A)$ satisfying `Λ.IsJacobian`, and an object $O$ of `JZeroNeronObjectAtP N₀ p hpN₀ A hA Λ`. Assume the Hecke hypotheses `HeckeInputsAll` at levels $N_0p$ and $N_0$ together with pairwise commutation of the operators `heckeOperatorBar` at both levels. Then for every maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}$ of $\mathbb{T} = \mathrm{MvPolynomial}\ \mathrm{Nat.Primes}\ \mathbb{Z}$ containing the image of $p$, and every $x$ in $J_0(N_0p) = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the level-$N_0p$ modular function field over $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ which lies in `O.finPts p` — the subgroup generated by the $p$-torsion points whose associated section extends to the place $A$ — is annihilated by $\mathfrak{m}$ for the module structure `heckeModuleBar (N₀ * p)`, and does not lie in `O.toricPts p` (the subgroup generated by the toric points of $O$ at $p$), the conclusion `HasLowerLevelTorsion (primesOf (N₀ * p)) 𝔪 (JZero N₀)` holds: there is a non-zero $y \in J_0(N_0)$, for the module structure `heckeModuleBar N₀`, killed by every integer lying in $\mathfrak{m}$ and by every element $T_\ell - b$ of $\mathfrak{m}$ with $\ell$ a prime not dividing $N_0p$ and $b \in \mathbb{Z}$.
--
--   This is the level-lowering step at $p$ in Ribet's analysis of the mod-$p$ reduction of $J_0(N_0p)$: a non-toric $\mathfrak{m}$-torsion point in the finite part of the Néron object at $p$ produces non-trivial $\mathfrak{m}$-torsion already at level $N_0$, with the same Hecke eigenvalues away from the primes of $N_0p$. It feeds the construction of the data used in Mazur's principle, being cited by [`ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.exists_jZeroNeronAtPDataOrdV22_toric_eq_fin_eq_of_forall_smul_sub_mem`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.exists_jZeroNeronAtPDataOrdV22_toric_eq_fin_eq_of_forall_smul_sub_mem).
